dist/

# Everything a shelf holds is generated, and none of it ever belongs in git. A
# Seed and a held Lens are immutable and digest-named, so keeping them means a new
# file every time either is written down, and a recorded reading is a cache that
# regenerates from the two.
#
# Matched wherever they land rather than per shelf. Naming one shelf's paths is
# how 34MB of another repository's corpus reached a pull request: the shelf moves
# with COMPLY_SHELF, and a rule that has to be extended for each new one is a rule
# that is one shelf behind.
**/seeds/
**/runs/
**/lens-versions/
